WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.644
What if all the ice on Earth melted?

2
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:08.290
Floating sea ice would barely change a thing. It’s already in the water.

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:14.478
But Greenland’s ice sits on land. Melted, it would raise the seas about seven metres.

4
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.650
Antarctica holds far more. About fifty-eight metres.

5
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:23.211
Add the mountain glaciers, and the seas rise roughly seventy metres.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.506
Beaches, ports and many coastal cities would be under water.

7
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.215
It wouldn’t happen overnight. It would likely take thousands of years.

8
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.828
For now, that ice is what holds our coastlines in place.
